{"id":"fidel-9936f5f350","am":"Family words are some of the first words children learn. እናት (enat) is mother, አባት (abat) is father, እህት (ehit) is sister, ወንድም (wendim) is brother, አያት (ayat) is grandparent, and ልጅ (lij) is child. Many families also say እማዬ (emaye) for Mom and አባዬ (abaye) for Dad.","ctx":"English lesson text containing Amharic words: check the Amharic words, transliterations and meanings"}
