{"id":"fidel-f0659c3e1c","am":"Amharic has its own punctuation marks. ። (arat netib, “four dots”) ends a sentence, like a period. ፣ (netela serez) separates words in a list, like a comma. A question ends with ? in modern writing. Old writing put ፡ (two dots) between every word instead of a space.","ctx":"English lesson text containing Amharic words: check the Amharic words, transliterations and meanings"}
