{"id":"fidel-2b33d1100e","am":"Describing words tell what something is like. Many come in opposite pairs: ትልቅ (tilik) big and ትንሽ (tinish) small; ሙቅ (muk) hot and ቀዝቃዛ (kezkaza) cold; ረጅም (rejim) tall or long and አጭር (achir) short; አዲስ (addis) new and አሮጌ (aroge) old.","ctx":"English lesson text containing Amharic words: check the Amharic words, transliterations and meanings"}
